    { t: "Work Lead-Safe in an Older Home", intro: "Disturbing lead paint creates dust that is especially harmful to children.", steps: ["Assume paint in pre-1978 homes contains lead unless tested.", "Post warning signs and keep occupants out of the work area.", "Cover floors and furniture with plastic and seal vents and doorways.", "Use wet scraping and sanding methods and HEPA-equipped tools.", "Clean up with a HEPA vacuum and wet wiping, not dry sweeping.", "Verify cleaning and document work as required."], tip: "Dry sanding and open-flame burning of lead paint are prohibited. Wet methods keep dust down." }
